# Powers agent/scoring.py (LLM scoring), agent/fixgen.py (fix generation),
# and agent/orchestrator.py (agentic tool-use loop). Uses any OpenAI-
# compatible endpoint; defaults to Mistral's hosted models.
# Without this, `main.py score` falls back to an offline heuristic scorer
# (fix generation and the orchestrator have no offline fallback and will
# error clearly if called without a key). `main.py scan` and `main.py eval`
# never need this at all.
MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# To point at a different OpenAI-compatible provider (Groq, Together,
# Fireworks, a local vLLM/Ollama server, ...) instead of Mistral, set these
# (LLM_API_KEY/LLM_BASE_URL take precedence over MISTRAL_API_KEY/GROQ_API_KEY):
# LLM_API_KEY=
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# LLM_SCORING_MODEL=mistral-small-latest
# LLM_FIX_MODEL=codestral-latest
# LLM_ORCH_MODEL=mistral-small-latest
# LLM_REVIEW_MODEL=mistral-small-latest

# Minimum seconds between LLM calls (client-side pacing to avoid tripping
# per-minute rate limits). Default 1.0; raise it if you're still hitting 429s.
# LLM_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1.0

# RAG (rag/get_standards) needs no key or setup -- it's a local, dependency-free
# TF-IDF retrieval index over rag/standards.py's corpus (see rag/index.py).
